[9.753183, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/FEATURES.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[9.754784, "o", "# Churn model features: specification\r\n\r\nOwner: retention data science. This is the contract between the feature pipeline (`python -m churn.build_features`)\r\nand the churn model (`python -m churn.train`). The live scoring service computes the same features from the same\r\ndefinitions, so offline and live values must agree.\r\n\r\n## The one rule\r\nEach output row is one prediction for one customer at one moment `t` (the row's `as_of`). **A feature for that row may\r\nuse only information that existed strictly before `t`.** The definitions below say exactly what that means for each\r\nfeature; where they are more specific, they win.\r\n\r\n"]
[9.754866, "o", "## Conventions\r\n- All timestamps are UTC, written as ISO 8601 with a `Z` suffix and whole seconds (`2025-03-04T06:00:00Z`).\r\n- \"Day\" means a UTC calendar date. `date(t)` is the UTC date of `t`.\r\n- \"In days\" means elapsed seconds divided by 86,400 (a fractional number).\r\n- `W days` means exactly `W × 86,400` seconds.\r\n- Windows are half-open: `[t − W days, t)` contains an event at exactly `t − W days` and does **not** contain an event at\r\n  exactly `t`. Events are stamped to the second, and an event stamped exactly at `t` (for example the box charge that\r\n  the 06:00 billing run creates while the 06:00 scoring run is reading) is not visible to the prediction at `t`.\r\n\r\n## Input tables (`--data <dir>`)\r\n| File | Columns | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n"]
[9.75492, "o", "| `customers.csv` | `customer_id, signup_at, plan, postcode_district` | one row per customer |\r\n| `scoring_points.csv` | `customer_id, as_of, trigger, app_minutes_7d` | one row per prediction; `(customer_id, as_of)` is unique; `trigger` is `batch` (the 06:00 run) or `ticket` (scored by the support desk when a ticket is opened, at the ticket's `opened_at`); `app_minutes_7d` is the product-analytics reading for that prediction and is often empty (export outages, devices offline) |\r\n| `orders.csv` | `order_id, customer_id, ordered_at, kind, amount_cents` | `kind` is `box` or `addon`; amounts are integer cents |\r\n| `tickets.csv` | `ticket_id, customer_id, opened_at, topic` | support tickets |\r\n| `status_snapshots.csv` | `customer_id, snapshot_date, status` | `snapshot_date` is a date (`YYYY-MM-DD`); at most one row per `(customer_id, snapshot_date)`; a snapshot dated `D` records the account status at the **end** of day `D`; `status` is one of `active`, `paused`, `payment_failed`, `cancelled` |\r\n| `labels.csv` | `"]
[9.754965, "o", "customer_id, as_of, churned_30d, label_available_at` | one row per labelled prediction; `churned_30d` is 1 if the customer cancelled in `(as_of, as_of + 30 days]`, else 0; `label_available_at` is when that outcome landed in the warehouse. Predictions whose outcome had not landed when the extract was taken have no row. |\r\n\r\n## Output (`--out <file.parquet>`)\r\nOne row per row of `scoring_points.csv`, exactly once each, with these columns (row and column order do not matter):\r\n\r\n| Column | Type | Definition |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `customer_id` | integer | key, from `scoring_points.csv` |\r\n| `as_of` | timestamp (UTC) | key, `t` |\r\n| `orders_7d` | integer | number of orders with `t − 7 days ≤ ordered_at < t` |\r\n| `orders_30d` | integer | number of orders with `t − 30 days ≤ ordered_at < t` |\r\n| `spend_30d_cents` | integer | sum of `amount_cents` over the same 30-day window; `0` when there are none |\r\n| `tickets_30d` | integer | number of tickets with `t − 30 days ≤ opened_at < t` |\r\n| `days_since_last_ord"]
[9.755028, "o", "er` | float or null | `t` minus the latest `ordered_at` that is `< t`, in days; null when the customer has no earlier order |\r\n| `tenure_days` | float | `t − signup_at`, in days |\r\n| `status` | string or null | `status` of the customer's latest snapshot with `snapshot_date < date(t)`; null when there is none. (The snapshot dated `date(t)` describes the end of that day, so it does not exist yet at `t`.) |\r\n| `app_minutes_7d` | float or null | the row's own `app_minutes_7d` when present; otherwise the value of the same customer's most recent row with a strictly earlier `as_of` that has one; otherwise null. Never a value from a row at or after `t`. |\r\n| `te_district` | float | target encoding of the customer's `postcode_district`, defined below |\r\n\r\n### `te_district`\r\nA label row is **available at `t`** when its `label_available_at < t`. For a prediction at `t` for a customer in\r\ndistrict `k`:\r\n- `p` = the mean of `churned_30d` over all label rows available at `t` (every district, every customer); if no label "]
[9.755081, "o", "row\r\n  is available at `t`, `p = 0.05`.\r\n- `n` = the number of label rows available at `t` whose customer is in district `k` (this includes the same customer's\r\n  own earlier predictions whose outcome has landed); `s` = the sum of their `churned_30d`.\r\n- `te_district = (s + 20 × p) / (n + 20)`  (a smoothed mean with prior weight `m = 20`).\r\n\r\n## Run time\r\nA run on an extract of the size in `/app/data` (about 3,000 customers) must finish within the limit stated in the task\r\nticket.\r\n"]
[9.755241, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[9.755316, "o", "root@a1227658-4fa7-4bbe-860c-4345cc3e1321:/app# "]
[10.105103, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/build_features.py\n"]
[10.105645, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/build_features.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[10.107987, "o", "\"\"\"Build the churn feature table: python -m churn.build_features --data <dir> --out <file.parquet>\"\"\"\r\nimport argparse\r\nimport os\r\n\r\nfrom churn.encoding import district_encoding\r\nfrom churn.impute import fill_app_minutes\r\nfrom churn.extract import load_extract\r\nfrom churn.status import latest_status\r\nfrom churn.windows import activity_features, tenure_days\r\n\r\nFEATURE_COLUMNS = [\"orders_7d\", \"orders_30d\", \"spend_30d_cents\", \"tickets_30d\", \"days_since_last_order\",\r\n                   \"tenure_days\", \"status\", \"app_minutes_7d\", \"te_district\"]\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[10.108011, "o", "def build(data_dir):\r\n    t = load_extract(data_dir)\r\n    points = t[\"scoring_points\"].reset_index(drop=True)\r\n    feats = activity_features(points, t[\"orders\"], t[\"tickets\"])\r\n    feats[\"tenure_days\"] = tenure_days(points, t[\"customers\"])\r\n    feats[\"status\"] = latest_status(points, t[\"status_snapshots\"])\r\n    feats[\"app_minutes_7d\"] = fill_app_minutes(points)\r\n    feats[\"te_district\"] = district_encoding(points, t[\"labels\"], t[\"customers\"])\r\n    return feats[[\"customer_id\", \"as_of\"] + FEATURE_COLUMNS]\r\n"]
[10.108075, "o", "\r\n\r\ndef main():\r\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--data\", required=True, help=\"folder with the extract CSVs\")\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", required=True, help=\"output parquet file\")\r\n    a = ap.parse_args()\r\n    feats = build(a.data)\r\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(a.out)), exist_ok=True)\r\n    feats.to_parquet(a.out, index=False)"]
[10.108215, "o", "\r\n    print(f\"wrote {len(feats)} rows x {feats.shape[1]} columns to {a.out}\")\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    main()\r\n"]
[10.108472, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[10.108531, "o", "root@a1227658-4fa7-4bbe-860c-4345cc3e1321:/app# "]
[13.41956, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/windows.py\n"]
[13.419743, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' churn/windows.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[13.423028, "o", "\"\"\"Activity features over trailing windows (orders, spend, tickets) and simple time-since features.\"\"\"\r\nimport numpy as np\r\nimport pandas as pd\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _daily(points, events, ts_col, amount_col=None):\r\n    \"\"\"Per customer and UTC day: number of events (and amount). Days that have a prediction but no event get 0.\"\"\"\r\n    ev = events.assign(day=events[ts_col].dt.floor(\"D\"))\r\n    agg = {\"n\": (ts_col, \"size\")}\r\n    if amount_col:\r\n        agg[\"amount\"] = (amount_col, \"sum\")\r\n    per_day = ev.groupby([\"customer_id\", \"day\"]).agg(**agg).reset_index()\r\n    pred_days = points[[\"customer_id\"]].assign(day=points[\"as_of\"].dt.floor(\"D\")).drop_duplicates()\r\n    grid = pd.concat([per_day[[\"customer_id\", \"day\"]], pred_days]).drop_duplicates()\r\n    daily = grid.merge(per_day, on=[\"customer_id\", \"day\"], how=\"left\").fillna(0)\r\n    return daily.sort_values([\"customer_id\", \"day\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _rolling(daily, cols, window):\r\n    # daily buckets keep this fast; the window covers the last `window` including the "]
[13.423109, "o", "prediction day\r\n    rolled = (daily.set_index(\"day\").groupby(\"customer_id\")[cols]\r\n              .rolling(window, closed=\"both\").sum().reset_index())\r\n    return rolled\r\n\r\n\r\ndef activity_features(points, orders, tickets):\r\n    out = points[[\"customer_id\", \"as_of\"]].copy()\r\n    out[\"day\"] = out[\"as_of\"].dt.floor(\"D\")\r\n\r\n    od = _daily(points, orders, \"ordered_at\", \"amount_cents\")\r\n    r7 = _rolling(od, [\"n\"], \"7D\").rename(columns={\"n\": \"orders_7d\"})\r\n    r30 = _rolling(od, [\"n\", \"amount\"], \"30D\").rename(columns={\"n\": \"orders_30d\", \"amount\": \"spend_30d_cents\"})\r\n    td = _daily(points, tickets, \"opened_at\")\r\n    t30 = _rolling(td, [\"n\"], \"30D\").rename(columns={\"n\": \"tickets_30d\"})\r\n    for part in (r7, r30, t30):\r\n        out = out.merge(part, on=[\"customer_id\", \"day\"], how=\"left\")\r\n    for c in (\"orders_7d\", \"orders_30d\", \"spend_30d_cents\", \"tickets_30d\"):\r\n        out[c] = out[c].fillna(0).astype(\"int64\")\r\n\r\n    # time since the last order strictly before the prediction\r\n    o = orders.sort_values(\"ordered_a"]
[13.423137, "o", "t\")[[\"customer_id\", \"ordered_at\"]]\r\n    left = out[[\"customer_id\", \"as_of\"]].reset_index().sort_values(\"as_of\")\r\n    last = pd.merge_asof(left, o, left_on=\"as_of\", right_on=\"ordered_at\", by=\"customer_id\",\r\n                         allow_exact_matches=False).set_index(\"index\").sort_index()[\"ordered_at\"]\r\n    out[\"days_since_last_order\"] = (out[\"as_of\"] - last).dt.total_seconds() / 86400\r\n    return out.drop(columns=[\"day\"])\r\n\r\n\r\ndef tenure_days(points, customers):\r\n    signup = points[\"customer_id\"].map(customers.set_index(\"customer_id\")[\"signup_at\"])\r\n    return (points[\"as_of\"] - signup).dt.total_seconds() / 86400\r\n"]
[13.423336, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[13.42339, "o", "root@a1227658-4fa7-4bbe-860c-4345cc3e1321:/app# "]
